<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Wix xmlns="http://wixtoolset.org/schemas/v4/wxs"
     xmlns:util="http://wixtoolset.org/schemas/v4/wxs/util">
  <!-- v1.0.4 (2026-08-15): ProductCode changed to auto-assigned (*). The previous fixed ProductCode was
       the root cause of "installing the new version prompts that the old version must be uninstalled first"
       (error 1638) — an identical ProductCode is treated as the same product, so MajorUpgrade never had
       a chance to run. With auto ProductCode + stable UpgradeCode + MajorUpgrade, double-clicking the new
       MSI performs a smooth in-place upgrade (RemoveExistingProducts removes the old and installs the new)
       with no duplicate install entries. The Package Version is extracted by the build script from
       FileVersion in Directory.Build.props and passed in via -d UnloseVersion, keeping assembly version
       and MSI version incremented from the same source.
       v1.0.3.1 (2026-08-07): added deepcode-cli command-line match detection (hosted by node.exe) and
       the QoderCN process name.
       v1.0.3 (2026-08-07): removed the "Pause protection 30 min" button from the home page (CLI keeps
       pause); agent status aggregated by application (ZCode × N instead of per-process); session PID
       reuse defense (process name + start time validation).
       2026-08-15: switched to self-contained single-file publishing (PublishSingleFile); a clean Win10
       no longer needs the .NET 8 runtime preinstalled. All managed DLL components were removed; added
       e_sqlite3.dll for UI/MCP/CLI, the 5 WPF native DLLs for UI, amd64\KernelTraceControl.dll /
       msdia140.dll and rules\danger_commands.yaml for Service (the rules file had never shipped in the
       package before; fixed here).
       v1.0.5 (2026-08-15): added AllowSameVersionUpgrades to MajorUpgrade — MSI only honors the first
       three version fields (official docs state the fourth is ignored), so four-part 1.0.4.0/1.0.4.1 are
       both 1.0.4 to MSI; the exclusive VersionMax boundary made FindRelatedProducts miss the old version,
       and side-by-side double installs were observed in testing.
       Fix: MSI ProductVersion uses only the first three fields (truncated in the bat) + same-version
       in-place reinstall allowed. Releases must bump the third field; the fourth field is a build marker only.
       2026-08-15: shortcuts given an explicit Target (without it they degrade to pointing at the install
       directory, opening a folder on click); added LaunchUiAfterInstall (launch into the tray right after
       install; asyncNoWait prevents installer hangs) and KillResidentProcesses (terminate UI/MCP resident
       processes before InstallValidate, fixing the Restart Manager 2803 error dialog during upgrades —
       closes VM task A observation item 2).
       2026-08-15 (multilingual): added a bilingual install dialog (language radio buttons, default follows
       OS via UserLanguageID; the choice is written to HKLM\Software\unlose\UILanguage for the UI to read on
       first launch); shortcuts use the neutral name unlose; service Description switched to English;
       downgrade prompt is bilingual. Package language stays 2052 — dialog text is inline bilingual,
       no multi-language transforms.
       v1.0.9 (2026-08-16): error 2803 recurred when upgrading with the service running — the kill CA
       terminated UI/MCP but not unlose.Service.exe, whose loaded image locks the file at InstallValidate
       and makes the Restart Manager demand the MsiRMFilesInUse dialog. Fix: the kill CA now stops the
       service too (graceful sc stop + taskkill backstop; the new package's ServiceControl restarts it),
       and MsiRMFilesInUse/FilesInUse dialogs are packaged as a safety net so any residual lock (a live
       CLI session, antivirus) degrades to a proper dialog instead of the 2803 error box.
       v1.0.9.3 (2026-08-17): (1) all console-exe custom actions (sc stop / ping / taskkill / sc failure)
       replaced by a single in-process .NET Framework 4.8 DTF DLL (Unlose.SetupActions) calling SCM/process
       APIs directly — the exe CAs flashed console windows on the desktop and HideTarget did not stop it;
       (2) ProgressDlg controls got the mandatory Subscribe wiring (SetProgress/ActionText EventMapping),
       without which the progress bar and the step line never update at all.
       v1.0.9.7 (2026-08-17): (1) every engine built-in ActionText line on our paths is overridden with
       the bilingual property pair — zh built-ins like “正在发布产品信息” read as if the installer were
       publishing something, so RegisterProduct/PublishFeatures/PublishProduct now show “正在注册产品信息...”;
       (2) NudgeInitialProgress (immediate, after InstallInitialize) advances the bar ~5% via the
       ProgressAddition + ProgressReport message pair so the long script/validate phase no longer reads
       as "not started"; (3) the cmd.exe uninstall-cleanup relay became a DTF CA (CreateNoWindow spawn),
       making the installer 100% shell-free. -->
  <Package Name="unlose" Version="$(var.UnloseVersion)"
           Manufacturer="unlose Team"
           ProductCode="*"
           UpgradeCode="146A322C-DE98-4193-A711-47E0CCDFFDA6"
           Language="2052" Codepage="936">

    <MajorUpgrade AllowSameVersionUpgrades="yes"
                  DowngradeErrorMessage="已安装更新版本的 unlose。 / A newer version of unlose is already installed." />
    <MediaTemplate EmbedCab="yes" />
    <!-- Product icon shown in Add/Remove Programs -->
    <Icon Id="AppIcon" SourceFile="$(var.Unlose.UI.TargetDir)Resources\unlose.ico" />
    <Property Id="ARPPRODUCTICON" Value="AppIcon" />
    <!-- Icon for the brand area of the language-selection dialog (Icon control references the Binary table) -->
    <Binary Id="BrandIconBin" SourceFile="$(var.Unlose.UI.TargetDir)Resources\unlose.ico" />

    <!-- UI language: install-time language-selection dialog; default follows the OS display language
         (UserLanguageID primary language id 4 = all Chinese LCIDs). The choice is written to
         HKLM\Software\unlose\UILanguage; the UI resolves it as "manual selection > install selection > OS language".
         Silent installs are covered too (SetProperty first does not depend on the UI layer).
         The UILANG property is named with no baseline value: UserLanguageID is a system property and
         command-line overrides are ineffective (VM test: UserLanguageID=1033 still got reset to 2052 by
         the engine), so a "Not UILANG" guard makes `msiexec UILANG=en` an explicit admin override.
         Definition order is execution order: Chinese override first, English fallback next, then dialog text. -->
    <!-- MSI condition syntax has no bitwise operators; Chinese LCIDs enumerated: 2052 zh-CN / 1028 zh-TW / 3076 zh-HK / 5124 zh-MO / 4100 zh-SG -->
    <Property Id="UILANG" Secure="yes" />
    <SetProperty Id="UILANG" Action="SetUILang_Zh" Value="zh" Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition="(UserLanguageID=2052 Or UserLanguageID=1028 Or UserLanguageID=3076 Or UserLanguageID=5124 Or UserLanguageID=4100) And Not UILANG" />
    <SetProperty Id="UILANG" Action="SetUILang_En" Value="en" Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition="Not UILANG" />

    <!-- Dialog text follows the OS language itself (not bilingual side by side): control Text references
         [properties]; the baseline is English and conditional SetProperty overrides it with Chinese. -->
    <Property Id="DlgTitleText" Value="Please select UI language" />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgTitleText" Action="SetDlgTitleTextZh" Value="请选择界面语言" Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgInstallText" Value="Install" />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgInstallText" Action="SetDlgInstallTextZh" Value="安装" Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgCancelText" Value="Cancel" />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgCancelText" Action="SetDlgCancelTextZh" Value="取消" Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <!-- One-line intro (the product name "unlose" is a brand name, constant in both languages, hardcoded directly) -->
    <Property Id="DlgIntroText" Value="File-safety protection: automatic snapshots for every AI session, restore anytime" />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgIntroText" Action="SetDlgIntroTextZh" Value="文件安全防护：每次 AI 会话自动快照，误删误改随时还原" Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />

    <!-- Progress-dialog title (stays on screen while the install executes) -->
    <Property Id="DlgInstallingText" Value="Installing unlose..." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgInstallingText" Action="SetDlgInstallingTextZh" Value="正在安装 unlose..." Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />

    <!-- Files-in-use dialog texts (MsiRMFilesInUse / FilesInUse). The engine shows these dialogs on demand
         when a process still holds a file at InstallValidate; without them it aborts with error 2803.
         The kill CA stops our own processes first, so the dialogs are a safety net for external locks. -->
    <Property Id="DlgFilesInUseTitleText" Value="Files in use" />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgFilesInUseTitleText" Action="SetDlgFilesInUseTitleZh" Value="文件被占用" Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgFilesInUseBodyText" Value="The following programs are using files that need to be updated. The installer can close them now and restart them after setup." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgFilesInUseBodyText" Action="SetDlgFilesInUseBodyZh" Value="以下程序正在使用需要更新的文件。安装程序可以先关闭它们，并在安装完成后自动重启。" Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgRestartAppsText" Value="Automatically close and restart the programs" />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgRestartAppsText" Action="SetDlgRestartAppsZh" Value="自动关闭这些程序，并在安装后重启" Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgOkText" Value="OK" />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgOkText" Action="SetDlgOkTextZh" Value="确定" Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <!-- Checkbox default: let the Restart Manager shut the locking apps down and restart them after install -->
    <Property Id="FileInUseProcessShutdown" Value="1" />

    <!-- Action-text lines for the progress dialog ([ActionText]): the engine looks up each action's
         description in the ActionText table when the action starts. Without these the line stays empty
         and the dialog looks frozen outside the short file-copy bursts (the progress bar itself only
         moves while files are copied — engine built-in behavior). -->
    <Property Id="DlgActValidating" Value="Preparing installation..." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgActValidating" Action="SetDlgActValidatingZh" Value="正在准备安装..." Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgActStoppingService" Value="Stopping the protection service..." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgActStoppingService" Action="SetDlgActStoppingServiceZh" Value="正在停止保护服务..." Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgActClosingWindows" Value="Closing unlose windows..." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgActClosingWindows" Action="SetDlgActClosingWindowsZh" Value="正在关闭 unlose 窗口..." Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgActCopying" Value="Copying files..." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgActCopying" Action="SetDlgActCopyingZh" Value="正在复制文件..." Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgActRemovingOld" Value="Removing the older version..." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgActRemovingOld" Action="SetDlgActRemovingOldZh" Value="正在移除旧版本..." Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgActStartingService" Value="Starting the protection service..." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgActStartingService" Action="SetDlgActStartingServiceZh" Value="正在启动保护服务..." Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgActConfiguringService" Value="Configuring service recovery..." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgActConfiguringService" Action="SetDlgActConfiguringServiceZh" Value="正在配置服务恢复策略..." Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgActInitializing" Value="Initializing installation..." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgActInitializing" Action="SetDlgActInitializingZh" Value="正在初始化安装..." Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgActFinalizing" Value="Finalizing installation..." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgActFinalizing" Action="SetDlgActFinalizingZh" Value="正在完成安装..." Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />

    <!-- The engine ships built-in localized ActionText for the standard actions; the zh-CN built-ins read
         e.g. “正在发布产品信息” for RegisterProduct/PublishProduct (owner found the wording misleading —
         the step registers the product). The overrides below replace every built-in line that shows on
         our install/upgrade paths with the bilingual property pair, so the step line never falls back to
         an engine string. -->
    <Property Id="DlgActRegistering" Value="Registering product information..." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgActRegistering" Action="SetDlgActRegisteringZh" Value="正在注册产品信息..." Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgActCleaningOld" Value="Cleaning up the older version..." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgActCleaningOld" Action="SetDlgActCleaningOldZh" Value="正在清理旧版本..." Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgActRemovingFiles" Value="Removing older files..." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgActRemovingFiles" Action="SetDlgActRemovingFilesZh" Value="正在移除旧文件..." Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgActPreparingFolders" Value="Preparing folders and shortcuts..." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgActPreparingFolders" Action="SetDlgActPreparingFoldersZh" Value="正在准备文件夹与快捷方式..." Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgActWritingRegistry" Value="Updating registry and environment..." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgActWritingRegistry" Action="SetDlgActWritingRegistryZh" Value="正在更新注册表与环境..." Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgActNudging" Value="Preparing installation progress..." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgActNudging" Action="SetDlgActNudgingZh" Value="正在准备安装进度..." Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />

    <!-- Exit-dialog texts (shown after a successful first install) -->
    <Property Id="DlgSuccessTitleText" Value="Setup completed successfully" />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgSuccessTitleText" Action="SetDlgSuccessTitleZh" Value="安装成功" Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgSuccessText" Value="unlose is now installed and protecting your files in the background. The protection service starts automatically with Windows." />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgSuccessText" Action="SetDlgSuccessTextZh" Value="unlose 已安装完成，正在后台保护你的文件。保护服务随 Windows 自动启动。" Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgLaunchText" Value="Open unlose and check protection status" />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgLaunchText" Action="SetDlgLaunchTextZh" Value="打开 unlose 并查看保护状态" Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />
    <Property Id="DlgFinishText" Value="Finish" />
    <SetProperty Id="DlgFinishText" Action="SetDlgFinishTextZh" Value="完成" Sequence="both" Before="CostInitialize"
                 Condition='UILANG="zh"' />

    <!-- Exit-dialog checkbox: launch the app (main window, not tray-only) when checked. Default = checked. -->
    <Property Id="LAUNCH_ON_EXIT" Value="1" Secure="yes" />

    <UI Id="UnloseLanguageUI">
      <TextStyle Id="DlgFont" FaceName="Segoe UI" Size="8" />
      <TextStyle Id="DlgFontTitle" FaceName="Segoe UI" Size="9" Bold="yes" />
      <TextStyle Id="DlgFontBig" FaceName="Segoe UI" Size="11" Bold="yes" />
      <Property Id="DefaultUIFont" Value="DlgFont" />

      <!-- Brand side panel shared by both dialogs (blue gradient + logo + wordmark, generated by make-brand-panel.ps1).
           Path is repo-root relative: the build script runs wix from the repository root. -->
      <Binary Id="BrandPanelBin" SourceFile="src/Installer/brand-panel.bmp" />

      <!-- ActionText table: drives the [ActionText] line on ProgressDlg so the user always sees which step
           is running (stopping service / copying / removing old version / starting service).
           WiX v4 note: the property reference must go in the Message attribute — inner text is rejected
           (WIX0400). The engine formats [DlgActXxx] at runtime, so the zh SetProperty overrides apply. -->
      <ProgressText Action="InstallInitialize" Message="[DlgActInitializing]" />
      <ProgressText Action="NudgeInitialProgress" Message="[DlgActNudging]" />
      <ProgressText Action="InstallValidate" Message="[DlgActValidating]" />
      <ProgressText Action="PrepareUpgrade" Message="[DlgActStoppingService]" />
      <!-- Engine built-in zh lines replaced with our bilingual wording (registering not “发布”): -->
      <ProgressText Action="ProcessComponents" Message="[DlgActCleaningOld]" />
      <ProgressText Action="UnpublishFeatures" Message="[DlgActCleaningOld]" />
      <ProgressText Action="RemoveRegistryValues" Message="[DlgActCleaningOld]" />
      <ProgressText Action="RemoveShortcuts" Message="[DlgActCleaningOld]" />
      <ProgressText Action="RemoveEnvironmentStrings" Message="[DlgActCleaningOld]" />
      <ProgressText Action="RemoveFiles" Message="[DlgActRemovingFiles]" />
      <ProgressText Action="RemoveFolders" Message="[DlgActRemovingFiles]" />
      <ProgressText Action="StopServices" Message="[DlgActStoppingService]" />
      <ProgressText Action="CreateFolders" Message="[DlgActPreparingFolders]" />
      <ProgressText Action="InstallFiles" Message="[DlgActCopying]" />
      <ProgressText Action="CreateShortcuts" Message="[DlgActPreparingFolders]" />
      <ProgressText Action="WriteRegistryValues" Message="[DlgActWritingRegistry]" />
      <ProgressText Action="WriteEnvironmentStrings" Message="[DlgActWritingRegistry]" />
      <ProgressText Action="RemoveExistingProducts" Message="[DlgActRemovingOld]" />
      <ProgressText Action="InstallServices" Message="[DlgActStartingService]" />
      <ProgressText Action="StartServices" Message="[DlgActStartingService]" />
      <ProgressText Action="ConfigureServiceFailureActions" Message="[DlgActConfiguringService]" />
      <ProgressText Action="RegisterProduct" Message="[DlgActRegistering]" />
      <ProgressText Action="PublishFeatures" Message="[DlgActRegistering]" />
      <ProgressText Action="PublishProduct" Message="[DlgActRegistering]" />
      <ProgressText Action="InstallFinalize" Message="[DlgActFinalizing]" />

      <!-- ════════ Dialog 1: language selection (every interactive install: first install, upgrade, reinstall) ════════ -->
      <Dialog Id="LanguageDlg" Width="420" Height="280" Title="unlose Setup" NoMinimize="yes">
        <Control Id="BrandPanel" Type="Bitmap" X="0" Y="0" Width="130" Height="280" Text="BrandPanelBin" TabSkip="yes" />
        <Control Id="BrandIntro" Type="Text" X="150" Y="22" Width="252" Height="34"
                 Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="no" Text="[DlgIntroText]" />
        <Control Id="TopLine" Type="Line" X="150" Y="74" Width="262" Height="0" />
        <Control Id="DlgTitle" Type="Text" X="150" Y="86" Width="252" Height="16"
                 Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="no"
                 Text="{\DlgFontTitle}[DlgTitleText]" />
        <!-- Language names written in their own language is international convention; both entries are constant regardless of OS -->
        <Control Id="LangGroup" Type="RadioButtonGroup" X="162" Y="112" Width="240" Height="56"
                 Property="UILANG">
          <RadioButtonGroup Property="UILANG">
            <RadioButton Value="zh" X="0" Y="0" Width="230" Height="18" Text="中文（简体）" />
            <RadioButton Value="en" X="0" Y="26" Width="230" Height="18" Text="English" />
          </RadioButtonGroup>
        </Control>
        <Control Id="BottomLine" Type="Line" X="150" Y="246" Width="262" Height="0" />
        <Control Id="Install" Type="PushButton" X="238" Y="252" Width="94" Height="18"
                 Default="yes" Text="[DlgInstallText]">
          <!-- FRESHINSTALL marks that this UI flow is a first install (drives the ExitDlg below) -->
          <Publish Property="FRESHINSTALL" Value="1" />
          <Publish Event="EndDialog" Value="Return" />
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Cancel" Type="PushButton" X="340" Y="252" Width="66" Height="18"
                 Cancel="yes" Text="[DlgCancelText]">
          <Publish Event="EndDialog" Value="Exit" />
        </Control>
      </Dialog>

      <!-- ════════ Dialog 1.5: progress (shown while the install executes, between LanguageDlg and ExitDlg) ════════
           Modeless: required — the MSI engine drives the execute phase while this dialog is on screen.
           The Subscribe elements are the mandatory EventMapping wiring: the engine only feeds the bar and
           the step line to controls that subscribe (SetProgress → ProgressBar, ActionText → Text). Without
           them both stay frozen no matter what the ActionText table contains — that was the real "no
           progress" defect (fixed v1.0.9.3 after the ActionText table was added in v1.0.9.2). -->
      <Dialog Id="ProgressDlg" Width="420" Height="280" Title="unlose Setup" NoMinimize="yes" Modeless="yes">
        <Control Id="BrandPanel" Type="Bitmap" X="0" Y="0" Width="130" Height="280" Text="BrandPanelBin" TabSkip="yes" />
        <Control Id="InstallingTitle" Type="Text" X="150" Y="40" Width="252" Height="26"
                 Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="no" Text="{\DlgFontBig}[DlgInstallingText]" />
        <Control Id="ProgressBar" Type="ProgressBar" X="150" Y="96" Width="252" Height="15"
                 ProgressBlocks="yes" Text="ProgressDone">
          <Subscribe Event="SetProgress" Attribute="Progress" />
        </Control>
        <Control Id="ActionText" Type="Text" X="150" Y="120" Width="252" Height="36"
                 Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="no" Text="[ActionText]">
          <Subscribe Event="ActionText" Attribute="Text" />
        </Control>
        <Control Id="BottomLine" Type="Line" X="150" Y="246" Width="262" Height="0" />
        <Control Id="Cancel" Type="PushButton" X="340" Y="252" Width="66" Height="18"
                 Cancel="yes" Text="[DlgCancelText]">
          <!-- Cancel immediately (the MSI engine rolls back the install); consistent with LanguageDlg's Cancel -->
          <Publish Event="EndDialog" Value="Exit" />
        </Control>
      </Dialog>

      <!-- ════════ Dialog: Restart Manager files-in-use (shown on demand when a process still locks a file) ════════
           The engine populates the ListBox (Property=FileInUseProcess) with the locking process names itself.
           OK with the shutdown checkbox publishes RMShutdownAndRestart so RM closes the apps and restarts
           them after install; without the checkbox the install continues and may finish with a reboot.
           Packaging this dialog is what turns the old fatal 2803 error box into a recoverable prompt. -->
      <Dialog Id="MsiRMFilesInUse" Width="420" Height="280" Title="unlose Setup" NoMinimize="yes">
        <Control Id="BrandPanel" Type="Bitmap" X="0" Y="0" Width="130" Height="280" Text="BrandPanelBin" TabSkip="yes" />
        <Control Id="Title" Type="Text" X="150" Y="40" Width="252" Height="26"
                 Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="no" Text="{\DlgFontBig}[DlgFilesInUseTitleText]" />
        <Control Id="Body" Type="Text" X="150" Y="76" Width="252" Height="40"
                 Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="no" Text="[DlgFilesInUseBodyText]" />
        <Control Id="List" Type="ListBox" Property="FileInUseProcess" X="150" Y="124" Width="252" Height="76"
                 Disabled="yes" Sorted="yes" />
        <Control Id="RestartApps" Type="CheckBox" Property="FileInUseProcessShutdown" CheckBoxValue="1"
                 X="150" Y="210" Width="252" Height="16" Text="[DlgRestartAppsText]" />
        <Control Id="BottomLine" Type="Line" X="150" Y="246" Width="262" Height="0" />
        <Control Id="OK" Type="PushButton" X="238" Y="252" Width="94" Height="18"
                 Default="yes" Text="[DlgOkText]">
          <Publish Event="RMShutdownAndRestart" Value="0" Condition="FileInUseProcessShutdown" />
          <Publish Event="EndDialog" Value="Return" />
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Cancel" Type="PushButton" X="340" Y="252" Width="66" Height="18"
                 Cancel="yes" Text="[DlgCancelText]">
          <Publish Event="EndDialog" Value="Exit" />
        </Control>
      </Dialog>

      <!-- ════════ Dialog: legacy files-in-use (same safety net when RM is disabled, e.g. MSIRESTARTMANAGERCONTROL=Disable) ════════
           The engine fills the ListBox itself; per the InstallValidate docs the ListBox of the FilesInUse
           dialog must be associated with the FileInUseProcess property (a wrong property name makes the
           engine fail to populate the list, error 2262, observed in VM/host testing). OK continues (locked
           files are then replaced via a reboot), Cancel aborts the install. -->
      <Dialog Id="FilesInUse" Width="420" Height="280" Title="unlose Setup" NoMinimize="yes">
        <Control Id="BrandPanel" Type="Bitmap" X="0" Y="0" Width="130" Height="280" Text="BrandPanelBin" TabSkip="yes" />
        <Control Id="Title" Type="Text" X="150" Y="40" Width="252" Height="26"
                 Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="no" Text="{\DlgFontBig}[DlgFilesInUseTitleText]" />
        <Control Id="Body" Type="Text" X="150" Y="76" Width="252" Height="40"
                 Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="no" Text="[DlgFilesInUseBodyText]" />
        <Control Id="List" Type="ListBox" Property="FileInUseProcess" X="150" Y="124" Width="252" Height="96"
                 Disabled="yes" Sorted="yes" />
        <Control Id="BottomLine" Type="Line" X="150" Y="246" Width="262" Height="0" />
        <Control Id="OK" Type="PushButton" X="238" Y="252" Width="94" Height="18"
                 Default="yes" Text="[DlgOkText]">
          <Publish Event="EndDialog" Value="Return" />
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Cancel" Type="PushButton" X="340" Y="252" Width="66" Height="18"
                 Cancel="yes" Text="[DlgCancelText]">
          <Publish Event="EndDialog" Value="Exit" />
        </Control>
      </Dialog>

      <!-- ════════ Dialog 2: exit / success (after a successful first install) ════════ -->
      <Dialog Id="ExitDlg" Width="420" Height="280" Title="unlose Setup" NoMinimize="yes">
        <Control Id="BrandPanel" Type="Bitmap" X="0" Y="0" Width="130" Height="280" Text="BrandPanelBin" TabSkip="yes" />
        <Control Id="SuccessTitle" Type="Text" X="150" Y="58" Width="252" Height="26"
                 Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="no"
                 Text="{\DlgFontBig}[DlgSuccessTitleText]" />
        <Control Id="SuccessText" Type="Text" X="150" Y="92" Width="252" Height="44"
                 Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="no" Text="[DlgSuccessText]" />
        <Control Id="LaunchCheckbox" Type="CheckBox" X="150" Y="152" Width="252" Height="18"
                 Property="LAUNCH_ON_EXIT" CheckBoxValue="1" Text="[DlgLaunchText]" />
        <Control Id="BottomLine" Type="Line" X="150" Y="246" Width="262" Height="0" />
        <Control Id="Finish" Type="PushButton" X="316" Y="252" Width="90" Height="18"
                 Default="yes" Cancel="yes" Text="[DlgFinishText]">
          <!-- Launch the main UI (not tray-only) as the installing user when the checkbox is on.
               Immediate CA in the UI sequence runs after ExecuteAction completed, so files exist.
               asyncNoWait: the UI process is long-lived; waiting would hang the installer. -->
          <Publish Event="DoAction" Value="LaunchAppOnExit" Condition="LAUNCH_ON_EXIT" />
          <Publish Event="EndDialog" Value="Return" />
        </Control>
      </Dialog>

      <InstallUISequence>
        <!-- Language selection shows on every interactive install run: first install, cross-version upgrade
             AND same-version double-click reinstall (owner decision 2026-08-17: re-running the MSI should
             feel like a full install, and the dialog doubles as the place to change the UI language).
             NOT Installed alone would skip it on same-version reinstalls (Installed=true then); the
             maintenance modes that must stay quiet are ARP repair (REINSTALL set) and uninstall
             (REMOVE="ALL"). Silent installs (/qn) never show dialogs regardless. -->
        <Show Dialog="LanguageDlg" Before="ExecuteAction" Condition="NOT REMOVE=&quot;ALL&quot; AND NOT REINSTALL" />
        <!-- Progress dialog: stays on screen during the whole execute phase so the user always sees
             "Installing unlose..." instead of a vanished window (the engine updates the progress bar). -->
        <Show Dialog="ProgressDlg" Before="ExecuteAction" />
        <!-- Success dialog after the install completes; shown whenever the LanguageDlg flow ran
             (FRESHINSTALL is set by the LanguageDlg Install button: first install, upgrade, reinstall).
             Silent installs (/qn) never show it. -->
        <Show Dialog="ExitDlg" OnExit="success" Condition="FRESHINSTALL" />
      </InstallUISequence>
    </UI>

    <!-- Launches unlose.UI.exe (main window) after the user clicks Finish on the exit dialog.
         Declared at Package level (a UI element may not contain CustomAction children);
         the ExitDlg Finish button references it via Publish DoAction. -->
    <CustomAction Id="LaunchAppOnExit" Directory="INSTALLFOLDER"
                  ExeCommand='"[INSTALLFOLDER]unlose.UI.exe"'
                  Execute="immediate" Impersonate="yes" Return="asyncNoWait" />

    <Feature Id="ProductFeature" Title="unlose" Level="1">
      <ComponentGroupRef Id="ProductComponents" />
      <ComponentGroupRef Id="ServiceComponents" />
      <ComponentGroupRef Id="StartupComponents" />
    </Feature>

    <!-- Reference custom actions defined in standalone Fragments, or the linker drops them entirely
         (the CA would not be included in the package and would not run on uninstall) -->
    <CustomActionRef Id="UninstallGuardCleanup" />
    <!-- INST-001 tiered service-failure recovery; previously never packaged for the same missing-reference reason, added here too -->
    <CustomActionRef Id="ConfigureServiceFailureActions" />
  </Package>

  <Fragment>
    <StandardDirectory Id="ProgramFiles64Folder">
      <Directory Id="INSTALLFOLDER" Name="unlose">
        <!-- Native subdirectories produced by self-contained single-file publishing: TraceEvent's amd64\*.dll and the dangerous-command rules yaml -->
        <Directory Id="ServiceAmd64Folder" Name="amd64" />
        <Directory Id="ServiceRulesFolder" Name="rules" />
      </Directory>
    </StandardDirectory>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment>
    <ComponentGroup Id="ProductComponents" Directory="INSTALLFOLDER">
      <Component Id="UIExe" Bitness="always64">
        <File Source="$(var.Unlose.UI.TargetDir)unlose.UI.exe" KeyPath="yes" />
      </Component>
      <!-- Shortcuts live in their own per-user components (ICE43/ICE57: non-advertised shortcuts need an
           HKCU registry KeyPath and cannot be mixed into per-machine file components).
           Explicit Target is required: when the component KeyPath is a registry value rather than a file,
           a shortcut without Target degrades to pointing at the install directory (click opens a folder
           instead of launching the app) — hit in local testing.
           Name is uniformly the brand name unlose: language-neutral, so English-locale users never see
           Chinese in the Start menu. -->
      <Component Id="StartMenuShortcut" Guid="D4E5F6A7-B8C9-0123-DEF0-123456789ABC" Bitness="always64">
        <Shortcut Id="StartMenuShortcut" Directory="ProgramMenuFolder"
                  Name="unlose" Target="[INSTALLFOLDER]unlose.UI.exe"
                  WorkingDirectory="INSTALLFOLDER" Icon="AppIcon" />
        <RegistryValue Root="HKCU" Key="Software\unlose\Shortcuts"
                       Name="StartMenu" Type="integer" Value="1" KeyPath="yes" />
      </Component>
      <Component Id="DesktopShortcut" Guid="E5F6A7B8-C9D0-1234-EF01-23456789ABCD" Bitness="always64">
        <Shortcut Id="DesktopShortcut" Directory="DesktopFolder"
                  Name="unlose" Target="[INSTALLFOLDER]unlose.UI.exe"
                  WorkingDirectory="INSTALLFOLDER" Icon="AppIcon" />
        <RegistryValue Root="HKCU" Key="Software\unlose\Shortcuts"
                       Name="Desktop" Type="integer" Value="1" KeyPath="yes" />
      </Component>
      <Component Id="InstallLanguage" Bitness="always64">
        <RegistryValue Root="HKLM" Key="Software\unlose" Name="UILanguage"
                       Type="string" Value="[UILANG]" KeyPath="yes" />
      </Component>
      <Component Id="CliExe" Bitness="always64">
        <File Source="$(var.Unlose.Cli.TargetDir)unlose.exe" KeyPath="yes" />
      </Component>
      <Component Id="McpServerExe" Bitness="always64">
        <File Source="$(var.Unlose.McpServer.TargetDir)unlose.McpServer.exe" KeyPath="yes" />
      </Component>
      <!-- Self-contained single-file: all managed assemblies are embedded in the exes; only the native
           DLLs accompanying each exe need packaging. The UI's 5 WPF native DLLs; the e_sqlite3.dll copies
           from all four products are identical and install to the root, so a single component
           (see ServiceSupport6 in ServiceComponents) avoids component GUID / short-filename conflicts. -->
      <Component Id="UiNative1" Bitness="always64"><File Source="$(var.Unlose.UI.TargetDir)D3DCompiler_47_cor3.dll" KeyPath="yes" /></Component>
      <Component Id="UiNative2" Bitness="always64"><File Source="$(var.Unlose.UI.TargetDir)PenImc_cor3.dll" KeyPath="yes" /></Component>
      <Component Id="UiNative3" Bitness="always64"><File Source="$(var.Unlose.UI.TargetDir)PresentationNative_cor3.dll" KeyPath="yes" /></Component>
      <Component Id="UiNative4" Bitness="always64"><File Source="$(var.Unlose.UI.TargetDir)vcruntime140_cor3.dll" KeyPath="yes" /></Component>
      <Component Id="UiNative5" Bitness="always64"><File Source="$(var.Unlose.UI.TargetDir)wpfgfx_cor3.dll" KeyPath="yes" /></Component>
      <!-- Path-B reachability: append the install directory to the system PATH so AI agents can invoke
           `unlose snapshot` from the injected instructions directly -->
      <Component Id="PathEnvironment" Guid="C3D4E5F6-A7B8-9012-CDEF-123456789012" Bitness="always64" KeyPath="yes">
        <Environment Id="UnlosePathEnv" Name="PATH" Action="set" Part="last" System="yes" Permanent="no"
                     Value="[INSTALLFOLDER]" />
      </Component>
      <!-- Tray icon: installed at the install root (the UI checks unlose.ico in the root first, then the Resources subdirectory) -->
      <Component Id="TrayIconFile" Bitness="always64">
        <File Source="$(var.Unlose.UI.TargetDir)Resources\unlose.ico" KeyPath="yes" />
      </Component>
    </ComponentGroup>

    <ComponentGroup Id="ServiceComponents" Directory="INSTALLFOLDER">
      <Component Id="ServiceExe" Guid="A1B2C3D4-E5F6-7890-ABCD-EF1234567890" Bitness="always64">
        <File Id="ServiceExeFile" Source="$(var.Unlose.Service.TargetDir)unlose.Service.exe" KeyPath="yes" />
        <!-- Service name is uniformly unloseService, consistent with Program.cs -->
        <ServiceInstall
          Id="unloseServiceInstall"
          Name="unloseService"
          DisplayName="unlose"
          Description="File-safety protection and snapshot management powered by VSS shadow copies"
          Type="ownProcess"
          Start="auto"
          ErrorControl="normal"
          Account="LocalSystem" />
        <!-- Write the basic recovery action types first; precise delays are overwritten by the post-install sc.exe failure CA. -->
        <util:ServiceConfig
          ServiceName="unloseService"
          FirstFailureActionType="restart"
          SecondFailureActionType="restart"
          ThirdFailureActionType="restart"
          ResetPeriodInDays="1"
          RestartServiceDelayInSeconds="5" />
        <ServiceControl Id="StartService" Name="unloseService" Start="install" Stop="both" Remove="uninstall" Wait="yes" />
      </Component>
      <!-- Self-contained single-file: managed assemblies (including TraceEvent/Serilog/YamlDotNet/SQLitePCL etc.)
           are all embedded in unlose.Service.exe; only the native companion files need packaging. -->
      <Component Id="ServiceSupport6" Bitness="always64"><File Source="$(var.Unlose.Service.TargetDir)e_sqlite3.dll" KeyPath="yes" /></Component>
      <Component Id="ServiceAmd64_1" Directory="ServiceAmd64Folder" Bitness="always64"><File Source="$(var.Unlose.Service.TargetDir)amd64\KernelTraceControl.dll" KeyPath="yes" /></Component>
      <Component Id="ServiceAmd64_2" Directory="ServiceAmd64Folder" Bitness="always64"><File Source="$(var.Unlose.Service.TargetDir)amd64\msdia140.dll" KeyPath="yes" /></Component>
      <!-- Dangerous-command rules file: old MSIs never packaged rules\danger_commands.yaml (latent defect); fixed here -->
      <Component Id="ServiceRulesFile" Directory="ServiceRulesFolder" Bitness="always64"><File Source="$(var.Unlose.Service.TargetDir)rules\danger_commands.yaml" KeyPath="yes" /></Component>
    </ComponentGroup>

    <!-- INST-003 fix: register the UI to auto-start on user logon -->
    <ComponentGroup Id="StartupComponents" Directory="TARGETDIR">
      <Component Id="UIStartup" Guid="B2C3D4E5-F6A7-8901-BCDE-F12345678901">
        <!-- tray parameter: at boot auto-start the UI only stays in the tray without opening the main window -->
        <RegistryValue Root="HKCU"
                       Key="Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run"
                       Name="unlose"
                       Value='"[INSTALLFOLDER]unlose.UI.exe" --tray'
                       Type="string"
                       KeyPath="yes" />
      </Component>
    </ComponentGroup>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment>
    <!-- In-process managed custom actions (src/Unlose.SetupActions: .NET Framework 4.8 + WiX DTF).
         CLR 4.x ships with every supported Windows, so the CA DLL runs prerequisite-free on clean
         machines; the app binaries are self-contained .NET 8 and cannot serve as an installer-side
         dependency. A DllEntry CA executes inside msiexec and spawns no process, which is why the
         console-exe CAs (sc stop / ping / taskkill / sc failure) moved here: they flashed console
         windows on the desktop and HideTarget did not suppress them (host test, v1.0.9.2 build). -->
    <Binary Id="UnloseSetupActions" SourceFile="$(var.Unlose.SetupActions.CAPath)" />

    <!-- INST-001 fix: implements the tiered recovery policy — restart after 5s on 1st/2nd failure, after
         60s on the 3rd — via ChangeServiceConfig2 (SCM API) instead of a `sc.exe failure` console CA. -->
    <CustomAction
      Id="ConfigureServiceFailureActions"
      BinaryRef="UnloseSetupActions"
      DllEntry="ConfigureServiceFailureActions"
      Execute="deferred"
      Impersonate="no"
      Return="ignore" />

    <InstallExecuteSequence>
      <Custom Action="ConfigureServiceFailureActions" After="StartServices" Condition='NOT REMOVE="ALL"' />
      <!-- Post-install app launch moved to the ExitDlg checkbox (LaunchAppOnExit, UI sequence):
           a visible "Setup completed" dialog with an "Open unlose" option replaces the old silent
           tray auto-start. Silent installs (/qn) start nothing — appropriate for deployment. -->
    </InstallExecuteSequence>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment>
    <!-- Uninstall cleanup (patent claim 11): on uninstall, the CLI asks the service to remove the guard
         instruction blocks from each user's global memory files via the paired markers and remove the
         deployed unlose-snapshot skill packs, restoring the original content with no residue.
         Scheduled before StopServices: the service is still running so the pipe is reachable; the SYSTEM
         context can write to every user directory; Return=ignore means failures never block uninstall;
         not triggered during major upgrade (MajorUpgrade removing the old version) — the new service takes over the blocks.
         v1.0.9.7: the cmd.exe relay became an in-process DTF CA that spawns the CLI itself with
         CreateNoWindow (the old HideTarget exe CA could still flash a console window; the installer is
         now 100% shell-free). INSTALLFOLDER arrives via CustomActionData; output still goes to
         C:\ProgramData\unlose\ca-cleanup.log for troubleshooting. -->
    <SetProperty Id="UninstallGuardCleanup" Value="[INSTALLFOLDER]" Sequence="execute"
                 Before="UninstallGuardCleanup" Condition='REMOVE="ALL" AND NOT UPGRADINGPRODUCTCODE' />
    <CustomAction
      Id="UninstallGuardCleanup"
      BinaryRef="UnloseSetupActions"
      DllEntry="UninstallGuardCleanup"
      Execute="deferred"
      Impersonate="no"
      Return="ignore" />

    <!-- Stop resident lock holders early (immediate, before InstallValidate): Restart Manager checks for
         files in use during InstallValidate; if unlose.UI.exe (tray/main window), unlose.McpServer.exe (a
         long-lived stdio process launched by the agent host) or the unloseService host process is still
         running, a full-UI install shows the MsiRMFilesInUse/FilesInUse dialogs (packaged since v1.0.9;
         without them the engine pops error 2803). The dialogs are the safety net; this CA is the first
         line so the common upgrade path shows no dialog at all.
         Policy (unchanged through the iterations): the service must be stopped gracefully via SCM first —
         a bare process kill would be counted as a crash and the INST-001 recovery policy would restart it
         seconds later, re-locking the file mid-install; the process kill is only a backstop for leftovers.
         unlose.exe (CLI) is deliberately not killed, to avoid interrupting an ongoing agent session — a
         live CLI degrades to the packaged MsiRMFilesInUse dialog instead of 2803.
         v1.0.9.3: the old three exe CAs (sc stop / ping wait / taskkill) became one in-process managed CA
         (SCM + Process APIs): same behavior, zero spawned processes, zero console windows. Per-machine
         installs run elevated, so the CA can stop the service and kill processes in any session; it never
         fails the install (nothing running on a fresh install is the normal case). -->
    <CustomAction
      Id="PrepareUpgrade"
      BinaryRef="UnloseSetupActions"
      DllEntry="PrepareUpgrade"
      Execute="immediate"
      Return="ignore" />

    <!-- Owner feedback (2026-08-17): the bar sits at 0% through script/validate/prepare and the install
         feels like it never started. This immediate CA fires right after InstallInitialize (the engine
         has just reset the bar with its master tick total) and nudges it ~5% via the documented
         ProgressAddition + ProgressReport message pair — see ManagedActions.NudgeInitialProgress. -->
    <CustomAction
      Id="NudgeInitialProgress"
      BinaryRef="UnloseSetupActions"
      DllEntry="NudgeInitialProgress"
      Execute="immediate"
      Return="ignore" />

    <InstallExecuteSequence>
      <Custom Action="UninstallGuardCleanup" Before="StopServices" Condition='REMOVE="ALL" AND NOT UPGRADINGPRODUCTCODE' />
      <!-- Resident-lock cleanup must complete before InstallValidate's Restart Manager file-lock check. -->
      <Custom Action="PrepareUpgrade" Before="InstallValidate" />
      <Custom Action="NudgeInitialProgress" After="InstallInitialize" />
    </InstallExecuteSequence>
  </Fragment>
</Wix>
